# =============================================================================
# Repo-root .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# The Docker build CONTEXT for every service is the repo ROOT (see any
# services/<svc>/Dockerfile for why — go.work needs sibling modules). This file
# keeps that context small: the daemon only receives the source the build needs,
# which speeds uploads and prevents cache busting from unrelated file churn.
#
# RULE OF THUMB: ignore everything that is NOT Go source / module manifests /
# migrations. The Dockerfile COPYs paths explicitly, so an over-broad ignore here
# would silently break the build — keep the "un-ignore" allowances below in mind.
# =============================================================================

# --- Version control / CI metadata (never needed in an image) ---------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitattributes

# --- Build artifacts & binaries ---------------------------------------------
bin/
dist/
out/
**/*.exe
**/*.test

# --- Test / coverage output --------------------------------------------------
**/*.out
cover.out
cover.html
coverage*

# --- Local env & secrets (must NEVER enter an image layer) ------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Editor / OS / tooling junk ---------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# --- Node / frontend (Web UI lands in M4; not part of any Go service image) -
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# --- Docs, design, ADRs, plans (not runtime artifacts) ----------------------
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
# ...but keep CLAUDE.md out too (covered by *.md). Migrations are *.sql, not *.md,
# so they are NOT ignored and still copy into the image.

# --- Infra / deploy configs (built/applied outside the image) ---------------
deploy/
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.*.yaml
scripts/
.golangci.yml
.claude/

# --- Dockerfiles themselves (the build already has the one it needs) --------
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
